{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Traffluent collects nothing on its own. It records only the events your app tracks and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context your app turns on: every kind of automatic instrumentation and every standard enricher is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"opt in. It sends records only to the destinations your app gives a delivery, to endpoints your app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names. None of it is used for tracking as Apple defines it: no module links what it records with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other companies’ data, reads the advertising identifier, fingerprints the device, or works around"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the user’s consent or App Tracking Transparency. Every manifest declares "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyTracking"},{"type":"text","text":" as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" and lists no tracking domains."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each module that can produce data of one of Apple’s collected data types ships a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" declaring it. SwiftPM and Bazel both put it in a resource bundle named","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Traffluent_<Module>.bundle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which Xcode and rules_apple copy into your app, where Xcode’s privacy","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"report finds it. A module your app doesn’t link adds nothing to the report.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Required-reason-APIs","text":"Required-reason APIs","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No Traffluent module calls an API on Apple’s list of required-reason APIs, so every manifest’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is empty. The list’s categories are file timestamps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), system boot time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), disk space"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), active keyboards"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryActiveKeyboards","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") and user defaults"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). The modules that come nearest:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Module","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What it calls"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Why none is a required-reason API","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","type":"reference","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"swift-system’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"FileDescriptor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"open","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"read","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"write","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"seek","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"resize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"close","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), ","type":"text"},{"code":"fsync","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"unlink","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"FileManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"createDirectory","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"setAttributes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the file protection class), ","type":"text"},{"code":"contentsOfDirectory","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"isExcludedFromBackup","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It reads no file’s timestamps, size from "},{"code":"stat","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or the volume’s free space: a segment’s size is the offset "},{"code":"seek","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" returns at its end, and the store bounds itself by the bytes it has written."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"FileManager.fileExists","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data(contentsOf:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data.write(to:options:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"FileVersionStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"ProcessInfo.performExpiringActivity","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It reads and writes the version file’s contents, never its attributes."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sysctlbyname"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hw.machine"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"c